":"Aaron Butler"},{"id":"nmuvddibqhk4","text":"IBEW Local 234 Health & Welfare Trust: Submitted a request for APA to become a participating behavioral health provider for the Trust. Highlighted APA’s behavioral health services, California footprint, and Salinas-area availability, and requested clarification on whether contracting should be completed directly with the Trust, through Anthem Blue Cross, or through another network/administrator.","at":"2026-10-05T14:53:16.934Z","by":"Aaron Butler"},{"id":"nmuvde8n8i2b","text":"IHP Network (Claritev): Submitted a request for APA to join the IHP Network as a participating behavioral health provider. Included APA’s practice information, California footprint, statewide telehealth capabilities, services, and provider capacity, and requested information regarding California participation, contracting, credentialing, reimbursement, and network requirements.","at":"2026-10-05T14:53:51.044Z","by":"Aaron Butler"},{"id":"nmuvdef1dyt8","text":"Imperial County Behavioral Health Services: Submitted a request for APA to become a contracted behavioral health provider with ICBHS. Included APA’s practice information and requested information regarding Medi-Cal enrollment, credentialing, contracting, reimbursement, and network participation requirements.","at":"2026-10-05T14:53:59.329Z","by":"Aaron Butler"},{"id":"nmuvdg5kmzis","text":"Contacted or pursued 19 unique leads today, including 13 network/contracting opportunities and 6 declined leads after review for relevance.\n\nContinued expanding APA’s potential contracting pipeline across IPAs, TPAs, TPNs, health plans, MPNs, employer health plans, and behavioral health networks, while prioritizing opportunities that align with APA’s California footprint and behavioral health services.","at":"2026-10-05T14:55:20.374Z","by":"Aaron Butler"},{"id":"nmuvdha13odh","text":"Declined the Healththopia lead after confirming that it is an ophthalmic clinic and therefore not relevant to APA’s behavio